<div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
<h3 itemprop="name">Can I sideload EPUBs without Wi-Fi?</h3>
<div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
<div itemprop="text">
<p>Yes. The X4 Classic has a magnetic pogo-pin data-and-charge port, so you can plug the device into a computer and drag EPUB, PDF, MOBI, or TXT files directly into the on-device storage. This is faster and more reliable than Wi-Fi transfer and avoids the need to set up an OPDS catalog or cloud sync. The 16 GB of internal storage plus a microSD card gives you room for tens of thousands of EPUBs.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
<h3 itemprop="name">Is the X4 Classic compatible with CrossPoint Reader firmware?</h3>
<div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
<div itemprop="text">
<p>As of September 9, 2026, CrossPoint 1.6.0 officially supports the Xteink X3, X4, X4 Pro, M5Stack PaperMono, Seeed reTerminal Sticky, and a few Waveshare reference boards — but not the X4 Classic. Because the X4 Classic uses an ESP32-S3 (the same chip family CrossPoint already targets), a future community port is plausible, but nothing has been announced. If you want CrossPoint today, the X4 Pro is the closest device in the XTEINK lineup with first-class CrossPoint support.</p>
</div>
